 983	\subsubsection{First Mover Advantage}
 984	\label{subsec:fma}
 985	In all contracts, \textit{P-Red} initiates the negotiation. In \cref{fig:fma}, we examine whether this confers an advantage by measuring the proportion of the negotiated resource (points in \PPC, tiles in \PTC) allocated to \textit{P-Red}.
 986	On \textit{Asymmetric} boards, \textit{P-Red} already holds a strategic advantage, so a higher share is expected. For \PPC, \textit{P-Red} secures around $60\%$ of the negotiated points even on \textit{Independent} and \textit{Mutually Dependent} boards, suggesting a first-mover advantage.
 987	In contrast, for \PTC, even on \textit{Asymmetric} boards allocations remain close to parity. 
 988	
 989	
